  "$comment": "Dwell's storybook palette (docs/ART_DIRECTION.md §2): the one source of colour for the painterly textures (shared/textures/materials.json) and the characters (shared/characters). A ramp is three painted values of one material: `shadow` (cooler, toward blue-violet), `base` (the local colour) and `light` (warmer, toward yellow). Reference a ramp stop as \"ramp.stop\" (\"meadow.light\"), a bare ramp name for its base, and a single swatch by its name (\"ink\"). Albedos stay inside about 0.06–0.92 in sRGB so the lights and ACES tone mapping keep them readable; the exceptions are the utility tiles' colours (`chalk`, white tinted by a state's colour or ruled as the sandbox grid, and the `missing_*` checker), which are not content. Run `node shared/textures/gen.mjs` after editing.",
